\title{ReticulateMuData}
\value{
A \code{ReticulateMuData} object
}
\description{
A MuData object backed by a Python \code{mudata.MuData} accessed through
\pkg{reticulate}. All data stay in Python; slots are converted on access.
Modalities are returned as \code{anndataR::ReticulateAnnData} objects (nested
MuData modalities as \code{ReticulateMuData}), so the shared \link{AbstractMuData}
interface works unchanged.

Python is only needed for this backend: native H5MU/Zarr reading and
writing never load it. \code{update()}, \code{pull_obs()}/\code{pull_var()},
\code{push_obs()}/\code{push_var()} and \code{copy()} call the Python implementation.

Refactored from the \code{ReticulateMuData} prototype in MofaflexR.
}
\section{Python access}{

\itemize{
\item \verb{$py_mudata()} returns the underlying Python object (\code{convert = FALSE})
\item \verb{$py_call(method, ...)} calls any Python method; \code{AnnData} and \code{MuData}
results are wrapped
}
}

